The poem juxtaposes physical momentum with existential risk, using Mario’s familiar cartoon world as a metaphor for human hesitation. The phrase "inertia of running" suggests that even when we move, we carry a resistance—an internal drag that can cause us to slip, much like Mario falling into the abyss. The line "skill issue" reframes failure not as a lack of ability but as a consequence of momentum, habit, or emotional inertia. It blends humor with melancholy: the absurdity of a video-game character falling is undercut by the seriousness of the emotional state it evokes. Overall, it reads as a compact meditation on how action can become a trap when we are too slow to adjust. [end of text]


